the trade fight. Main Senate choices set, and Ohio Statewide races get the long-telling

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:21.960
before the rest of the day and a strike abroad. People started voting Tuesday in contests

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.760
that set which party runs Congress through the last two years of President Trump's second

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:31.040
term. The New York Times and the Guardian both have that polling underway. Republicans are defending

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:36.560
a slim house edge, and Democrats need four more seats than they hold now. 35 Senate seats are

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:42.540
up, counting special elections in Florida and Ohio. Republicans have 53 senators, Democrats

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:47.800
and the independents who sit with them have 47. Taking the chamber means Democrats gain four seats

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.880
and keep every seat they already have. NBC News adds that at least two of those flips would have

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:58.060
to come in states. Mr. Trump carried by double digits in 2024. Governors are on the ballot

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:04.680
in 36 states in three US territories, 39 offices in all, plus state legislatures, local posts,

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:10.440
judges, and measures on taxes, abortion rights, and voting rules. The time says Mr. Trump has

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:14.960
told supporters to treat the day as if his own name were on the ballot and that he has insisted

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:20.500
Republicans win if his base shows up. Democratic campaigns have blamed him and his signature policies

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:25.100
for the strain of making ends meet. Republicans have tried to make the choice about opponents they

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:31.680
describe as radical, far-left activists. Add impact data, as the Times reports it, puts this midterm

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:38.780
as the costliest in political ads since at least 2018. Elon Musk put $474 million into Republican

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:44.380
candidates and their allies. The first polls close at 7 p.m. Eastern. Full results could take days

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:50.380
or weeks. In 2024, California's closest house races took three weeks. A federal judge

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:55.060
refused a request from Democratic lawmakers and party organizations to bar the administration

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:59.460
from pushing states to screen incoming ballots. The Supreme Court signaled it was not

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.700
interested in helping Mr. Trump interfere with how states run elections.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:08.000
The Guardian notes the president's party has lost house seats in 18 of the past 20 midterms,

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.600
back to 1946.

00:02:10.912 --> 00:02:14.232
Campabello Island, New Brunswick, holds about 900 people,

00:02:14.532 --> 00:02:16.552
and Global News says their only road bridge

00:02:16.552 --> 00:02:19.212
runs to Lou Beck main, not to the rest of Canada.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.352
No gas station sits on the island,

00:02:21.752 --> 00:02:25.172
and grocery shelves are thin, so everyday shopping means a border crossing.

00:02:25.732 --> 00:02:28.572
A student who lives there and goes to high school in the United States

00:02:28.572 --> 00:02:30.392
said she crosses almost every morning.

00:02:30.992 --> 00:02:34.432
Islanders paid a 25% tariff on U.S. goods they brought back

00:02:34.432 --> 00:02:36.472
until Ottawa carved out a special exemption.

00:02:36.472 --> 00:02:41.852
Last month, U.S. border officers turned a truckload of supplies around, and a local brewery

00:02:41.852 --> 00:02:43.172
has closed because of the tariffs.

00:02:43.832 --> 00:02:48.012
Canadian trips to Maine fell by half last year after President Trump's tons and tariffs.

00:02:48.592 --> 00:02:53.472
New Brunswick MP John Williamson said choices made in far-off capitals land on Campobello

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:53.912
at once.

00:02:54.492 --> 00:02:58.912
Lubbeck resident Nelson Meeker said there is no reason to stir bad blood between good neighbors.

00:02:59.552 --> 00:03:04.292
American fisherman Dana Barker, 50 years on the island with his Canadian wife, said the

00:03:04.292 --> 00:03:05.472
two sides will work it out.

00:03:05.472 --> 00:03:10.140
Maine Senate race sets incumbent Republicans Susan Collins against Democrat

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:15.280
Troy Jackson, a former state Senate president, PBS reports. Collins first

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:20.460
elected in 1996, once a sixth term. She is the only Republican senator from a

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:25.140
state vice president Kamala Harris won in 2024 and she won by nine points in

